{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfS5UKLzdExrt1ygRrRUG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, here's what I found:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment entity and enum: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27`\n- Shipment controller (no confirm endpoint yet): `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56`\n- Repository: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27`\n- Exception handling: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:11-30`\n- Error codes: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37`\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. REST endpoints throw `ApiException` subclasses (`ResourceNotFoundException`, `ConflictException`)\n2. HTTP status codes are set with `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.X).body(...)`\n3. All errors follow a standard envelope through `GlobalExceptionHandler`\n4. Error codes are enums that map to specific HTTP statuses (404→NOT_FOUND, 409→CONFLICT)\n5. Tests verify both status codes and error envelope structure with `jsonPath` assertions\n6. Repository methods return `Shipment?` (nullable) and are checked in controller\n\n**Affected files (cannot be avoided):**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add the `POST /{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` — must add new error code for invalid state (409 when CANCELLED)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for all four requirement cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking existing tests if endpoint routing interferes\n- Failing to handle the idempotent case (retry succeeds)\n- Missing the persistence requirement (actually update and save the shipment)\n- Inconsistent error codes vs. existing patterns\n\n**Open questions:**\n- For the 409 error when confirming a CANCELLED shipment, what error code? (I'll use `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to be specific about the state violation)\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment {\n       val shipment = repository.findById(shipmentId)\n           ?: throw ResourceNotFoundException(ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, \"No shipment with id '$shipmentId'\")\n       \n       return when (shipment.status) {\n           ShipmentStatus.CREATED -> {\n               val confirmed = shipment.copy(status = ShipmentStatus.CONFIRMED)\n               repository.save(confirmed)\n           }\n           ShipmentStatus.CONFIRMED -> shipment  // idempotent: already confirmed\n           ShipmentStatus.CANCELLED -> throw ConflictException(\n               ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE,\n               \"Cannot confirm a cancelled shipment\"\n           )\n       }\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** — Add error code for state violation:\n   - Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the `ErrorCode` enum (409 handled by `ConflictException`)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test cases:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED and returns 200\n   - Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds with 200 (idempotent)\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with error envelope\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with error envelope\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Reusing `VALIDATION_FAILED` (ErrorCode 400) — wrong HTTP status for this conflict\n- Creating a service layer — overkill for this simple state transition\n- Using `ResponseEntity<Shipment>` with explicit status — existing code doesn't do this pattern\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n1. **CREATED → CONFIRMED**: Read shipment, check status is CREATED, update status, save, return updated shipment (200)\n2. **CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED**: Read shipment, check status is CONFIRMED, return same shipment unchanged (200, idempotent)\n3. **CANCELLED shipment**: Read shipment, check status is CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException` with 409\n4. **Non-existent**: Try to read, get null, throw `ResourceNotFoundException` with 404\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Create a shipment (CREATED), confirm it, verify status is CONFIRMED in response\n- Test 2: Confirm the same shipment again, verify it still returns CONFIRMED (idempotent)\n- Test 3: Manually set a shipment to CANCELLED in the repository, confirm it, verify 409 and error code\n- Test 4: Attempt to confirm a non-existent shipment, verify 404 and error code\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Let me start by adding the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":837,"cache_read_input_tokens":20630,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":837},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"79559472-2581-4e82-9ba1-7ffe3d2bfb0a","uuid":"6257456e-216f-4ed2-a060-b0f5aba4415c","timestamp":"2026-09-26T12:49:24.238Z","request_id":"req_011CfS5UJuDVynA5r8BnchWA"}
